          "evidence_id": "70e2b07fea7043d1a9d76a3dc4034ebd@1053:2657",
          "quote": "It contains 80863 manually annotated pages from diverse data sources to represent a wide variability in layouts. For each PDF page, the layout annotations provide labelled bounding-boxes with a choice of 11 distinct classes."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "70e2b07fea7043d1a9d76a3dc4034ebd@3542:8093",
          "quote": "It provides pageby-page layout annotation ground-truth using bounding-boxes for 11 distinct class labels on 80863 unique document pages, of which a fraction carry double- or triple-annotations."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "70e2b07fea7043d1a9d76a3dc4034ebd@9269:15427",
          "quote": "DocLayNet contains 80863 PDF pages. Among these, 7059 carry two instances of human annotations, and 1591 carry three. This amounts to 91104 total annotation instances. The annotations provide layout information in the shape of labeled, rectangular boundingboxes. We define 11 distinct labels for layout features, namely Caption, Footnote, Formula, List-item, Page-footer, Page-header, Picture, Section-header, Table, Text, and Title."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "70e2b07fea7043d1a9d76a3dc4034ebd@19196:20609",
          "quote": "We reviewed the collected documents and identified the most common structural features they exhibit. This was achieved by identifying recurrent layout elements and lead us to the definition of 11 distinct class labels. These 11 class labels are Caption, Footnote, Formula, List-item, Pagefooter, Page-header, Picture, Section-header, Table, Text, and Title."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "queries": []
}

{
